-        // are COMMITTED (they have been streamed to the user; they are part of the answer)
-        // until mid turns READY or the front budget runs out. Readiness is polled at
-        // segment boundaries only -- no cv-wait inside generation, so a late mid costs at
-        // most one extra segment. The budget cap exists so a pathologically slow load
-        // cannot let the 135M write the entire answer.
+        // while the 4B arrives: it keeps producing seam-cut segments that are COMMITTED
+        // (they have been streamed to the user; they are part of the answer) until mid
+        // turns READY or the front budget runs out. Readiness is polled at segment
+        // boundaries only -- no cv-wait inside generation, so a late mid costs at most one
+        // extra segment. front_cap (above) is what stops a pathologically slow load from
+        // letting the 135M write the entire answer.
+        //
+        // NOT under --hard-mode verify. There the opener span becomes the verify seed, and
